# CLAUDE.md (work machine)

Thin top-level config. The portable rules live in the installed harness core;
this file imports them and holds only what is specific to this machine and this
job.

@CLAUDE.core.md

Both `CLAUDE.core.md` and `DISPATCH.core.md` are installed next to this file, so
the relative import above resolves. Read `DISPATCH.core.md` for the dispatch
contract; it is not auto-imported so that the core file stays usable on its own.

## Work overlay

Machine and employer specifics go here and nowhere else. Nothing in this
section is ever synced back to the harness repo.

Things worth filling in, once you know them:

- Where work repositories live on this machine, and which ones are in scope.
- Any directory the agent must never read or write.
- The team's build, test, and lint commands when they differ from the default.
- Review and approval rules that apply to this codebase.
- Who to ask when a policy question comes up.
